        <title>recipes:best_low-carb_coleslaw</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/best_low-carb_coleslaw?rev=1605745239&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Best Low-carb Coleslaw (Food.com)

	*  16 ounces shredded cabbage (about 1 small to medium cabbage)
	*  1 small onion, thinly sliced
	*  1/4 cup Splenda
	*  1/2 teaspoon salt
	*  1/2 teaspoon fresh ground black pepper
	*  1/2 cup mayonnaise
	*  1/2 cup whipping cream OR half-and-half OR buttermilk OR plain kefir
	*  1 1/2 tablespoons white vinegar
	*  2 1/2 tablespoons lemon juice</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/bisquick_substitute?rev=1599346828&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2020-09-05T19:00:28-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:bisquick_substitute</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/bisquick_substitute?rev=1599346828&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Bisquick® Substitute
Yield: 1 cup

INGREDIENTS
1 cup all-purpose flour
1 ½ teaspoons baking powder
¼ teaspoon salt
1 tablespoon butter

Step 1
Sift flour into a bowl; add baking powder and salt and whisk until fully incorporated. Cut butter into flour mixture using a pastry cutter until evenly combined.
Shortening or oil can be used in place of the butter, if desired. If using melted butter, be sure to evenly disperse the butter as much as possible.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/black_beans_and_rice?rev=1236715267&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2009-03-10T16:01:07-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:black_beans_and_rice</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/black_beans_and_rice?rev=1236715267&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Black Beans and Rice
 from “A Taste of Old Cuba”, by Maria Josefa LLuria de O'Higgins.

8 Servings

Ingredients: 
1. For cooking the beans:

	*  1 pound dry black beans
	*  2.5 quarts water
	*  1 green bell pepper, cored, seeded and cut into strips
	*  2 garlic cloves, peeled and lightly crushed but left whole
	*  1 large slice of onion (optional)</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/broccoli_with_asian_garlic_sauce?rev=1521305396&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2018-03-17T12:49:56-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:broccoli_with_asian_garlic_sauce</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/broccoli_with_asian_garlic_sauce?rev=1521305396&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Broccoli with Asian Garlic Sauce

Serves 4 as side serving

Ingredients

	*  4 cups broccoli florets and peeled stem slices
		*  3 garlic cloves, minced
		*  2 tablespoons sesame oil
		*  2 tablespoons soy sauce
		*  1/2 cup vegetable or chicken broth
		*  1 tablespoon cornstarch
		*  red pepper flakes to taste
		*  (1 can straw mushrooms or bamboo shoots or water chestnuts)</description>
    </item>
